#=GF CC   This domain is found in diverse bacterial signaling proteins.
#=GF CC   It is called EAL after its conserved residues. The EAL domain is
#=GF CC   a good candidate for a diguanylate phosphodiesterase function
#=GF CC   [1]. The domain contains many conserved acidic residues  that
#=GF CC   could participate in metal binding and might form the
#=GF CC   phosphodiesterase active site [1].
